# Versioning

When committing or preparing to push code changes, bump the patch version in `pyproject.toml` (`[project].version`).

A **pre-commit hook** (`scripts/bump_version.py`) auto-bumps the patch version when staged files include code changes. It updates `pyproject.toml` and stages it — no manual step needed.

## When to bump
- Bump on commits that include code changes (`.py`, config, tests, workflows, etc.)
- Do NOT bump for docs-only commits (README, markdown, comments-only)

## How to bump
- Increment the patch segment only: `0.1.17` → `0.1.18`
- Edit only `pyproject.toml` — no other version files exist
- Include the version bump in the same commit as the code changes (not a separate "version update" commit)
- If committing manually outside Cursor, run `pre-commit install` once so the hook runs automatically

## Before push
- If code changed since the last version bump, bump before pushing
- Do not push code changes without a corresponding version bump
